MANGA109, WHICH IS NOT A SOFTWARE LICENCE
-----------------------------------------

Three of the models above were trained on Manga109 or on annotations derived
from it. Manga109's images are distributed by its maintainers under terms of
their own, and those terms restrict use of the DATASET -- academic use, with
commercial use requiring a separate agreement.

Whether that reaches a MODEL somebody else trained on it, or the boxes such a
model draws on a page it has never seen, is not settled law anywhere. The
model publishers above license their weights MIT and GPL-3.0 respectively,
which is their statement about their own work.

This note exists so that whoever reads it later knows the question is there.
It is not legal advice and nobody here is a lawyer. If money is going to
change hands, ask one.


WHAT IS NOT COVERED BY ANY OF THIS
----------------------------------

The translation engines -- Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, OpenRouter and anything
else reached over HTTP -- are services, not code in this program. Their terms
are between the person running mangatl and the provider, and they are the one
part of the pipeline this file has nothing to say about.

The manga themselves are somebody's copyright. Nothing here grants any right
to them.
